  "goodToKnow": "Der Ruhestand is retirement: in den Ruhestand gehen (to retire), im Ruhestand sein (to be retired). It's slightly formal; in everyday speech Germans say in Rente gehen, or for civil servants in Pension gehen. The official age is gradually rising to 67. Der Unruhestand is a playful word for an active retirement. Literally, Ruhestand is the state of rest, from Ruhe (rest, quiet) and der Stand (state)."
